<<<

1351

+ Latin -sco are the i. terminations, as gignosko learn (i.e. come to know), calesco grow warm. The many English words in -esce, -escent, as recrudesce, iridescent, are from Latin ii.
===

+ Latin *-sco* are the i. terminations, as *gignōskō* learn (i. e. come to know), *calesco* grow warm. The many English words in *-esce*, *-escent*, as *recrudesce*, *iridescent*, are from Latin ii.
>>>

